e found;\n--   M.blob  — one whole value per key (cinterp's facts, CART-1299), string.buffer bytes written to a temp file and\n--             renamed; a value that would not come back equal is refused by name.\n-- A LOG holds one JSON array `[qkey, value]` per line, read back once per scope. Appending is atomic enough for one\n-- writer per scope; a torn last line is skipped on read.\n-- ⚠ THE KEY IS JSON-ENCODED, never written raw: LuaJIT's io.lines() MANGLES a line holding a NUL and glues it onto the\n-- NEXT line (measured: 'A\\0b\\t…' + 'plain\\t…' read back as one line 'Aplain\\t…'), and a layouts key is `T \\0 path` —\n-- every such answer missed, every run, while the log grew by the same answers.\n-- ⚠ NOTHING IS EVICTED: a changed input writes new entries beside the old ones (cpython's facts + layouts: ~5 MB a key\n-- set). Clearing the directory is always safe — it only costs a cold run.\n"},"verb":"edit","touched":["lua/cartograph/stampcache.lua"]},"verb":"edit"},{"id":"1790933182.089771-edit","invocation":{"args":{"file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md","before":"| Keep an EXPENSIVE answer across runs without ever serving a stale one — which inputs is it a function of, and is the cache invisible in the output? | `local SC = require 'cartograph.stampcache'` — `SC.key { part, … }` (sha256 of the parts, length-prefixed), `SC.file(path)` (a file's CONTENT hash, memoized per process — never an mtime: CART-1301), `SC.log(name, scope)` → `{ get(q) -> v, found; put(q, v) }` (one append-only log per scope key under `stdpath(cache)/cartograph/stamped/<name>/`; `false` is a stored \"none\", `found` tells it from a miss; any key bytes, NUL included — lines are JSON, a torn line is skipped). `CARTOGRAPH_STAMPCACHE=0` = a log that remembers nothing: the A/B. FIRST USER: cinterp's `layouts` fact (gcc offset/size probes) — the scope is the unit's text + flags + cwd + compiler identity + the CONTENT of every header in its include closure (written by the