, read back once per scope. Appending is atomic enough for one\n-- writer per scope; a torn last line is skipped on read.\n-- ⚠ THE KEY IS JSON-ENCODED, never written raw: LuaJIT's io.lines() MANGLES a line holding a NUL and glues it onto the\n-- NEXT line (measured: 'A\\0b\\t…' + 'plain\\t…' read back as one line 'Aplain\\t…'), and a layouts key is `T \\0 path` —\n-- every such answer missed, every run, while the log grew by the same answers.\n-- ⚠ NOTHING IS EVICTED: a changed input writes new entries beside the old ones (cpython's facts + layouts: ~5 MB a key\n-- set). Clearing the directory is always safe — it only costs a cold run.\n"},"verb":"edit","touched":["lua/cartograph/stampcache.lua"]},"bytes":936,"decided_by":"tactic"},{"id":"1790933182.089771-edit","decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"args":{"file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md","before":"| Keep an EXPENSIVE answer across runs without ever serving a stale one — which inputs is it a function of, and is the cache invisible in the output? | `local SC = require 'cartograph.stampcache'` — `SC.key { part, … }` (sha256 of the parts, length-prefixed), `SC.file(path)` (a file's CONTENT hash, memoized per process — never an mtime: CART-1301), `SC.log(name, scope)` → `{ get(q) -> v, found; put(q, v) }` (one append-only log per scope key under `stdpath(cache)/cartograph/stamped/<name>/`; `false` is a stored \"none\", `found` tells it from a miss; any key bytes, NUL included — lines are JSON, a torn line is skipped). `CARTOGRAPH_STAMPCACHE=0` = a log that remembers nothing: the A/B. FIRST USER: cinterp's `layouts` fact (gcc offset/size probes) — the scope is the unit's text + flags + cwd + compiler identity + the CONTENT of every header in its include closure (written by the probe compile's own `-MD`). MEASURED 2026-10-02 on the cpython gate: readings 200.6 s off / 200.6 cold / **45.0 warm** (wall 310 → 155 s), readings byte-identical in all three; store 660 KB. CART-1303 |\n","after":"| Keep an EXPENSIVE answer across runs without ever serving a stale one — which inputs is it a function of, and is the cache invisible in the output? | `local SC = require 'cartograph.stampcache'` — `SC.key { part, … }` (sha256 of the parts, length-prefixed), `SC.file(path)` (a file's CONTENT hash, memoized per process — never an mtime: CART-1301), `SC.log(name, scope)` → `{ get(q) -> v, found; put(q, v) }` (one append-only log per scope key under `stdpath(cache)/cartograph/stamped/<name>/`; `false` is a stored \"none\", `found` tells it from a miss; any key bytes, NUL included — lines are JSON, a torn line is skipped). `CARTOGRAPH_STAMPCACHE=0` = a log that remembers nothing: the A/B. FIRST USER: cinterp's `layouts` fact (gcc offset/size probes) — the scope is the unit's text + flags + cwd + compiler identity + the CONTENT of every header in its include closure (written by the probe compile's own `-MD`). MEASURED 2026-10-02 on the cpython gate: readings 200.6 s off / 200.6 cold / **45.0 warm** (wall 310 → 155 s), readings byte-identical in all three; store 660 KB. CART-1303 |\n| Are a runtime's interpreter FACTS re-derived on every gate run — which ones come from the store, which are refused and why? | Nothing to call: `require('cartograph.cinterp.facts').derive(tree)` answers each DERIVE CALL from the content-stamped blob store (`stampcache.blob 'facts'`) under a key of the tree's CONTENT (`stampcache.tree`: every file, 2.0 s for cpython's 417 MB), the scope, the toolchain (gcc + make identity), the derivation's CODE (its file + every cartograph module / sibling derivation its text requires or loads, read from the text) and each need's VALUE (`stampcache.value`, canonical); `T.cache` = `{ hits, stored, refused = { [derivation] = why }, stamp_ms }`, `T.rows[f].cached`. Refused by name, never stored: a function / userdata / metatable value (layouts' lookup, units' tree-sitter nodes), a value over a MB not worth its bytes (sources: 87 MB for 2 s), a derivation reading a `got` fact it does not declare, one that CHANGES a need (numbers-tvis → reps.tag: re-run every time, the need re-keyed). A gap or a raise is never stored. `CARTOGRAPH_STAMPCACHE=0` / `opts.cache = false` = everything derived (the A/B); `CARTOGRAPH_STAMPCACHE_DIR` moves the store (the suite's lives in its state home). MEASURED 2026-10-02, off → warm, output byte-identical in all four: cpython wall 307.7 → 103.6 s (facts 106.2 → 56.2, 11 hits; readings 199.2 → 45.1 with the layouts store), erlbif 121.4 → 80.5, qjs 17.2 → 13.5, cpath 65.9 → 57.0. The rest of cpython's facts is units' parse (45 s, not storable): CART-1321. CART-1299 |\n"},"verb":"edit","touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"]},"bytes":1566,"decided_by":"tactic"}],"hand":87}
